# B2 (CsCl) ordering target on BCC 4x4x4 = 128 atoms.
# Species: 0 = A, 1 = B.
#
# Warren-Cowley signature of B2:
#   shell 0 (NN, z=8): all unlike pairs (A's NN are all B and vice versa)
#                      -> alpha_AB = 1 - P(B|A)/c_B = 1 - 1/0.5 = -1
#   shell 1 (2NN, z=6): all like pairs (A's 2NN are all A; same sublattice)
#                      -> alpha_AB = 1 - 0/0.5 = +1
#
# Targeting both shells locks in B2 uniquely. Targeting only shell 0
# would also work since maximally-ordered NN for 50:50 BCC is unique
# (up to A<->B swap), but two-shell targeting helps the optimizer
# escape near-B2 antiphase boundaries faster.
SRO 0 1 0 -1.0
SRO 0 1 1 +1.0
